nd functional injection for complex parsing logic.\n  23 - **React Performance**: Optimized store access with atomic selectors and implemented memoization for the Report Builder sub-components.\n  24 \n  25 ### **Zone Tabs Layout & Production UI Overhaul**\n  26 **Date**: March 2026\n  27 **Summary**: Modernized the core document production workspace and unified the brand identity across the platform.\n  28 \n  29 - **3-Zone Architecture**: Transitioned the main generator to a professional 3-column \"IDE Pattern\" with persistent Top Identity, Left Setup, Center Document, and Right AI Context zones.\n  30 - **Manifest Interaction Model**: Redesigned all multi-step processes (Build, Export, Library) into technical manifests with activity-ready pulsing headers and data-dense bodies.\n  31 - **Professional Sidebar Density**: Standardized sidebar aesthetics with bold uppercase tracking and context-first hierarchies (e.g., reordering Context -> Prompt -> Controls).\n  32 - **Contextual HUDs**: Implemented semi-transparent floating glass-morphism HUDs for secondary utilities like Zoom and Syntax Guides.\n  33 - **Visual Identity Synchronization**: Unified the brand aesthetic across the Home Page, Global Header, and interactive Cover Page editor with high-fidelity textures and typography.\n  34 - **Writing Tools Overhaul**: Completed a high-fidelity modernization of flagship specialist tools (**Summarizer, Researcher, Stylist, Document Writer, Blueprint, Quiz, UI Description, Idea Generator, Lecture Generator, Session Plan, Assignments Solver**), transitioning them to the Manifest Workspace layout with technical setup panels and high-depth results canvases.\n  35 - **Admin Console Modernization**: Replaced the legacy admin interface with a professional 3-zone architecture, featuring technical HUD navigation, a sticky system status header, and manifest-style management consoles for Users, Payments, Templates, and RAG Ingestion.\n  36 \n  37 ## January 2026 Updates\n  38 \n  39 ### **RAG System & Production Readiness**\n  40 **Date**: January 2026\n  41 **Impact**: Critical - Core functionality enhancement\n  42 **Status**: \u2705 Completed\n  43 \n  44 **Features & Fixes**:\n  45 1. **Full RAG System Implementation**\n  46    - Integrated **Qdrant** as the production-ready vector database.\n  47    - Utilized **Ollama** with `nomic-embed-text` model for generating embeddings.\n  48    - Implemented a complete indexing pipeline (`indexer.ts`) for processing and vectorizing documents.\n  49    - Built a robust retrieval pipeline (`retrieval.ts`) with advanced filtering.\n  50 \n  51 2. **Admin RAG Tooling**\n  52    - Created a **Document Indexer** page for admins to upload and manage knowledge base files (PDF, DOCX, TXT).\n  53    - Developed a **RAG Query Tester** for real-time search testing with configurable parameters (topK, minScore, reranking).\n  54    - Added a **RAG Health Monitor** to check the status of Qdrant and Ollama services.\n  55 \n  56 3. **Advanced RAG Features**\n  57    - Implemented a multi-layer **caching system** for embeddings and search results, improving repeated query latency by over 90%.\n  58    - Added multiple **re-ranking strategies** (Hybrid, Cross-Encoder, BM25) to enhance search result quality.\n  59 \n  60 4. **Critical Configuration Fixes**\n  61    - Enabled strict mode for TypeScript and ESLint in `next.config.ts` to catch errors at build time.\n  62    - Centralized all environment variables into `src/lib/config.ts` with Zod validation.\n  63    - Removed all hardcoded IP addresses and configuration values.\n  64 \n  65 5. **State Management Overhaul**\n  66    - Refactored `useBuilderStore` to be more stable and client-centric.\n  67    - Implemented a clear status system (`loading`, `idle`, `dirty`, `saving`).\n  68    - Added a `useBeforeUnload` hook to prevent accidental loss of unsaved changes.\n  69    - Improved editor synchronization logic to be more reliable.\n  70 \n  71 6. **Guest Mode & UI Stability**\n  72    - Implemented a \"Continue as Guest\" feature for new users.\n  73    - Guest projects are persisted locally in IndexedDB.\n  74    - Disabled all credit-based and cloud-save features for guests.\n  75    - Stabilized the main `Header` component to prevent hydration mismatch errors.\n  76 \n  77 7. **Comprehensive Payment Management**\n  78    - Overhauled the admin settings page to allow full CRUD management of all payment methods (e-wallets, banks, etc.).\n  79    - Created a flexible data structure to support diverse payment types.\n  80    - Simplified the user-facing credit purchase dialog to use a dynamic credit amount slider instead of fixed plans.\n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/progress.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Progress Report - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 *Last Updated: March 2026*\n   3 \n   4 ## Development Milestones\n   5 \n   6 ### Phase 1: Foundation (Completed - Q3 2024)\n   7 \u2705 **Core Infrastructure**\n   8 \u2705 **Authentication System**\n   9 \u2705 **Initial AI Integration**\n  10 \n  11 ### Phase 2: Core Features (Completed - Q4 2024)\n  12 \u2705 **AI Writing Tools Suite** (23+ tools)\n  13 \u2705 **Document Generation System** (DOCX, PPTX)\n  14 \u2705 **User Management** (Admin Dashboard, RBAC)\n  15 \n  16 ### Phase 3: Advanced Features (Completed - Q4 2024)\n  17 \u2705 **Payment System** (Credit-based)\n  18 \u2705 **Multi-language Support** (EN/AR with RTL)\n  19 \u2705 **Admin Dashboard** (Analytics, User/Payment Management)\n  20 \n  21 ### Phase 4: Quality & Reliability (Completed - December 2024)\n  22 \u2705 **Document Export Reliability**: Comprehensive DOCX/PPTX export bug fixes.\n  23 \u2705 **Agent Lab Optimization**: SQLite backend, caching, and performance tuning.\n  24 \u2705 **Comprehensive Payment Management**: Full admin UI for all payment methods.\n  25 \n  26 ### Phase 5: RAG System & Production Readiness (Completed - January 2026)\n  27 \u2705 **RAG System Implementation**: Qdrant vector store, Ollama embedding models.\n  28 \u2705 **Admin RAG Tooling**: Document indexer, real-time query tester, health monitor.\n  29 \u2705 **Advanced RAG Features**: Multi-layer caching and hybrid re-ranking.\n  30 \u2705 **Critical Configuration Fixes**: Enabled strict modes, validated environment variables.\n  31 \u2705 **State Management Overhaul**: Implemented stable, client-side first state management with unsaved changes protection.\n  32 \u2705 **Guest Mode**: Implemented \"Continue as Guest\" feature with local persistence.\n  33 \n  34 ### Phase 6: Hardening & Expansion (Completed - March 2026)\n  35 \u2705 **API Documentation System**: Interactive, self-documenting API portal.\n  36 \u2705 **AI Project Consultant Chat**: In-app conversational AI to assist with project development.\n  37 \u2705 **Architectural Hardening**: Reached 100% Clean Architecture (DDD) compliance.\n  38 \u2705 **Firebase Client Decommissioning**: Fully migrated to local SQLite/Cookie-based auth and removed client-side SDKs.\n  39 \u2705 **Local File Storage**: Replaced Firebase Cloud Storage with local filesystem storage.\n  40 \u2705 **AI Infrastructure Refinement**: Categorized flows and unified tool schemas.\n  41 \u2705 **Zone Tabs Layout Implementation**: Modernized the main generator with a persistent 3-zone architecture.\n  42 \u2705 **Integrated Global AI Settings**: Moved behavioral rules and parameters to contextual sidebars.\n  43 \u2705 **Manifest Interaction Model**: Standardized multi-step operations into production-grade manifest dialogs.\n  44 \u2705 **Writing Tools Overhaul**: Completed a high-fidelity overhaul of flagship specialist tools (**Summarizer, Researcher, Stylist, Document Writer, Blueprint, Quiz, UI Description, Idea Generator, Lecture Generator, Session Plan, Assignments Solver**), transitioning them to the Manifest Workspace layout.\n  45 \u2705 **Admin Console Modernization**: Replaced the legacy admin interface with a professional 3-zone architecture and manifest-style management consoles for Users, Payments, Templates, and Document Indexing.\n  46 - \ud83d\udd04 **Test Coverage Expansion**: Increase unit and integration test coverage to 40%+.\n  47 - \ud83d\udd04 **Performance Monitoring**: Implement real-time monitoring.\n  48 - \ud83d\udd04 **Collaboration Features**: Begin development of team-based features.\n  49 \n  50 ### Phase 7: Scaling & Optimization (Current Focus)\n  51 \u2705 **AI Resilience Enhancement**: Implemented tiered model fallback and request timeouts for 8GB RAM stability.\n  52 \u2705 **Domain Entity Standardization**: Unified all domain entities on the `toProperties()` and `withProps()` pattern.\n  53 \u2705 **Client-Server SDK Decoupling**: Resolved critical bundling errors by isolating heavy AI SDKs from the browser.\n  54 - \ud83d\udd04 **RAG Retrieval Optimization**: Implement hybrid search and reranking improvements.\n  55 - \ud83d\udd04 **UI Performance**: Further optimize React rendering for the editor.\n  56 - \ud83d\udd04 **Enhanced Tooling**: Add specialized AI tools for academic research.\n  57 - \ud83d\udd04 **Mobile Experience Refinement**: Optimize the 3-zone architecture for smaller touch devices.\n  58 \n  59 \n  60 ## Feature Completion Status\n  61 \n  62 ### Writing Tools (23/23 - 100% Complete)\n  63 \u2705 All core writing tools are operational.\n  64 \n  65 ### Document Features (100% Complete)\n  66 \u2705 Report Generation, Presentation Builder, Document Export.\n  67 \n  68 ### RAG System (100% Complete)\n  69 \u2705 Semantic Search, Context-Aware Generation, Knowledge Base.\n  70 \n  71 ### Platform Features (100% Complete)\n  72 \u2705 User Authentication, Payment Processing, Multi-language Support, Admin Dashboard.\n  73 \u2705 **AI Project Consultant Chat**: In-app conversational AI to assist with project development.\n  74 \n  75 ### Developer Experience (New)\n  76 \u2705 **Interactive API Documentation**: A comprehensive, self-documenting portal for