2026-04-05 06:20:52.060 | 24908 (24908) | DEBUG    | Model request part: {"tool_name": "open_files", "content": ["Successfully opened AGENTS.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # AGENTS.md \u2014 Arkan Project Guide\n   1 \n   2 ## Overview\n   3 **Arkan** is an AI-powered academic and professional writing platform built with Next.js 15, TypeScript (strict mode), and Google Genkit. It follows Clean Architecture principles, utilizing Domain-Driven Design (DDD) to maintain strict separation between business logic and infrastructure.\n   4 \n   5 ## Subagents \u2014 Specialist Delegation\n   6 Delegate tasks to specialized subagents to ensure deeper focus and higher quality results. Subagent definitions are located in `.rovodev/subagents/`. Use the `invoke_subagents` tool to initiate delegation.\n   7 \n   8 ### Delegation Matrix\n   9 | Subagent | Primary Use Cases |\n  10 | :--- | :--- |\n  11 | **Next.js 15 AI/Server Actions** | App Router, data fetching, `use server` patterns, Genkit flows. |\n  12 | **shadcn/ui Builder** | UI components, Radix primitives, CVA, accessibility. |\n  13 | **Data Table/Dashboard** | Admin dashboards, TanStack Table, Recharts. |\n  14 | **Real-time/WebSocket** | SSE, WebSockets, streaming endpoints. |\n  15 | **State Management** | Zustand stores (`useBuilderStore`), state architecture. |\n  16 | **Bug Hunter** | Reproducing bugs, analyzing `errors.txt`, detailed reporting. |\n  17 | **Code Review/Best Practices** | Security audits, refactoring, code quality, consistency. |\n  18 | **Scalability Advisor** | RAG/Qdrant optimization, API bottleneck analysis. |\n  19 \n  20 *Pattern:* Always delegate new feature implementation by splitting tasks: **AI Dev** (logic) + **shadcn/ui** (component) + **Server Actions** (form handling).\n  21 \n  22 ---\n  23 \n  24 ## Architectural Patterns\n  25 \n  26 ### Clean Architecture (DDD)\n  27 Modules in `src/modules/` follow a standardized four-layer structure:\n  28 1. **`domain/`**: Pure entities, repository interfaces, and Zod schemas.\n  29 2. **`application/`**: Use cases orchestrating domain logic.\n  30 3. **`adapters/`**: API clients, controllers, and localized Zustand stores.\n  31 4. **`infrastructure/`**: Concrete implementations (Genkit, SQLite/Drizzle, Qdrant).\n  32 \n  33 ### Dependency Injection (DI)\n  34 *   **Registration**: Use `tsyringe` with `@injectable()`/`@inject()`. Register all services in `src/infrastructure/di/container.ts`.\n  35 *   **Server-Only Logic**: Use a `typeof window === 'undefined'` guard with `require()` inside `container.ts` to prevent client bundle contamination.\n  36 *   **Resolution**: Use the `useService(token)` hook in React components. Avoid `new` instantiation.\n  37 \n  38 ### AI & Genkit Flows\n  39 *   **Implementation**: All flows must be in `src/modules/ai/infrastructure/flows/` and prefixed with `'use server'`.\n  40 *   **Types & Schemas**: Use `z.enum` for strict typing; return results as `Result<T, E>` objects. Access values via `.getValue()`.\n  41 *   **Consistency**: Use `MODEL_BY_TASK` constants. Apply `cleanAiOutput` post-processing to strip AI conversational fillers (e.g., \"Sure, here is...\").\n  42 \n  43 ---\n  44 \n  45 ## Coding Conventions\n  46 *   **TypeScript**: Zero tolerance for `any`. Use `unknown` with narrowing.\n  47 *   **Components**: Default to Server Components; use `'use client'` only when necessary.\n  48 *   **Styling**: Tailwind CSS only. Use `cn()` for merging classes and CVA for variants.\n  49 *   **State**: Zustand for complex client UI; TanStack Query for server state.\n  50 *   **API**: Standardize responses using `handle*Result` helpers in `src/infrastructure/api/api-utils.ts` to ensure consistent status codes and telemetry.\n  51 \n  52 ---\n  53 \n  54 ## RAG & Infrastructure\n  55 *   **Vector Store**: Qdrant (`arkan_vectors` collection, 768 dimensions).\n  56 *   **Storage**: Local files via `storage/uploads/`. Protect endpoints with path-traversal checks.\n  57 *   **i18n**: Support for English (LTR) and Arabic (RTL) via `LanguageDirectionManager`.\n  58 \n  59 ---\n  60 \n  61 ## Change Log\n  62 *   **Consolidation**: Merged repetitive \"Important Files\" and \"Environment Variables\" into functional categories.\n  63 *   **Deduplication**: Removed redundant paragraphs regarding Genkit/Ollama configuration and DI patterns scattered throughout the original file.\n  64 *   **Structure**: Applied a logical hierarchy (Overview -> Subagents -> Architecture -> Coding -> Infrastructure).\n  65 *   **Refinement**: Removed filler text and consolidated contradictory instructions regarding file storage and architecture patterns into definitive guidelines.\n  66 *   **Formatting**: Standardized lists, tables, and code snippets for readability.\n````"], "tool_call_id": "pyd_ai_161575ea467c47ce89aca41a94bb7386", "metadata": null, "timestamp": "2026-04-05T06:20:52.059237+00:00", "part_kind": "tool-return"}
